## wiki auto refresh

This project maintains a lightweight semantic wiki under wiki_{{ project_name }}/ and refreshes it with the wiki engine update command.

When the user types /wiki-refresh, run python -m wiki_engine.cli update --project {{ project_name }} before doing anything else unless the user explicitly asks for read-only analysis.

Rules:
- For codebase questions, use query-first retrieval. If qmd is available, run qmd query "<question>" -c wiki_{{ project_name }} --json -n 10 before reading multiple markdown files.
- Load wiki_{{ project_name }}/templates/llm_wiki_workflow_guide.md before editing wiki content.
- Treat wiki refresh as incremental by default. Do not force broad re-reads of wiki_{{ project_name }}/ after every change; only load pages related to the current task.
- Dirty files under wiki_{{ project_name }}/ after refresh are expected. Do not skip refresh because wiki files are dirty unless the task is specifically about diagnosing refresh correctness.
- Use staged context loading to reduce tokens: (1) wiki_{{ project_name }}/index.md, (2) wiki_{{ project_name }}/templates/llm_wiki_workflow_guide.md before wiki edits, (3) folder-specific architecture/QA/decision notes only when they exist and are relevant to the changed module.
- When adding wiki knowledge that should help Graphifyy communities, include explicit code paths, symbols, config files/keys, and business rationale in the same note, for example `Target: src/models/forecasting.py -> run_forecast()` and `Config Parameter: volatility_penalty inside config.yaml`.
- Never browse wiki_{{ project_name }}/stage/ unless the user provides an exact file path.
- Prefer focused diffs and targeted file reads over full-file dumps or repo-wide scans.
- After code, config, or test edits that affect behavior or documentation semantics, run python -m wiki_engine.cli update --project {{ project_name }} once near completion to refresh artifacts.
- In the final response, report refresh status in one line: wiki_refresh: ran or wiki_refresh: skipped (<reason>).
